    "content": "{\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Improve the performance of the n-body simulation by utilizing OpenMP for parallel execution.\",\n  \"transformations\": [\"Add OpenMP directives to parallelize the body_force function.\", \"Optimize the loop order to improve cache utilization.\", \"Use a more efficient method to calculate the gravitational impact.\", \"Profile the code to identify bottlenecks and optimize them further.\"],\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"src/nbody.c\",\n      \"content\": \"/*\\n * Each body holds coordinate positions (i.e., x, y, and z) and\\n * velocities (i.e., vx, vy, and vz).\\n */\\ntypedef struct { float x, y, z, vx, vy, vz; } Body;\\n\\n/*\\n * Compute the gravitational impact among all pairs of bodies in \\n * the system.\\n */\\nvoid body_force(Body *p, float dt, int n) {\\n  #pragma omp parallel for\\n  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\\n    float fx = 0.0f; \\n    float fy = 0.0f; \\n    float fz = 0.0f;\\n\\n    #pragma omp parallel for\\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\\n      float dx = p[j].x - p[i].x;\\n      float dy = p[j].y - p[i].y;\\n      float dz = p[j].z - p[i].z;\\n      float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\\n      float inv_dist = 1 / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\\n      float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\\n\\n      fx += dx * inv_dist3; \\n      fy += dy * inv_dist3; \\n      fz += dz * inv_dist3;\\n    }\\n\\n    p[i].vx += dt*fx; \\n    p[i].vy += dt*fy; \\n    p[i].vz += dt*fz;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * Read a binary dataset with initilized bodies.\\n */\\nBody* read_dataset(int *nbodies) {\\n  int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\\n  if (b != 1) {\\n    fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError reading nbodie value\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n  }\\n  Body *bodies = (Body *)malloc(*nbodies * sizeof(Body));\\n  b = fread(bodies, *nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdin);\\n  if (b != 1) {\\n    fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError reading input values\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n  }\\n\\n  return bodies;\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * Write simulation results into a binary dataset.\\n */\\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, Body *bodies) {\\n  int b = fwrite(bodies, nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdout);\\n  if (b != 1) {\\n    fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError writing to output\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nint main(int argc,char **argv) {\\n  int nbodies;\\n\\n  Body *bodies = read_dataset(&nbodies);\\n\\n  /*\\n   * At each simulation iteration, interbody forces are computed,\\n   * and bodies' positions are integrated.\\n   */\\n  for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; iter++) {\\n    body_force(bodies, DT, nbodies);\\n\\n    #pragma omp parallel for\\n    for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; i++) {\\n      bodies[i].x += bodies[i].vx * DT;\\n      bodies[i].y += bodies[i].vy * DT;\\n      bodies[i].z += bodies[i].vz * DT;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  write_dataset(nbodies, bodies);\\n\\n  free(bodies);\\n\\n  exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\\n}\\n\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"This experiment aims to improve the performance of the n-body simulation by utilizing OpenMP for parallel execution. The body_force function is parallelized using the #pragma omp parallel for directive to distribute the workload across multiple threads. The loop order is optimized to improve cache utilization. The gravitational impact calculation is also optimized by calculating the square root and inverse distance only once per pair of bodies.\",\n  \"research\": {\n    \"queries\": [\n      \"What are the benefits of using OpenMP for parallelizing the n-body simulation?\",\n      \"How can I optimize the loop order to improve cache utilization in the n-body simulation?\"\n    ],\n    \"urls\": [\n      \"https://www.openmp.org/specs/latest/\",\n      \"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/parallelizing-loops-in-c-with-openmp/\"\n    ]\n  }\n}"
